From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:02:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Suggest only favorites with a video, only where the view
 plays one, and keep the panel steady

- Only a system view with a <video> bound to {system:continue:video} gets
  suggestions; with any other theme {system:continue}, hasContinue and X are
  as before (the best-rated favorite on a system never played).
- The pool: the favorites with a video. A system with favorites but none
  with a video gets no suggestion (its best-rated favorite); only a system
  with no favorite suggests its best-rated games with a video. Games of
  tools, emulators and screenshots and media under 1 KB are left out, so a
  collection never offers a tool to X.
- The list made again after a game changed keeps the current suggestion
  while it is still in it.
- A suggestion's video end moves on in the view's update, together with the
  panel's rebinding, and X starts the game the panel shows (should the
  suggestion have changed since it was bound, a menu on top, say). A
  suggestion stays at least 5 s: a video that ends at once loops until then.
- A system's slides wait for its theme, and the cards bind their slides
  again when the view shows and a list changed (a favorite added in a game
  list), without a tab change.
